{
  "name": "OperationalTask",
  "type": "object",
  "description": "CONTROL ROOM TASK SCHEDULING module: One record = one scheduled operational task \u2014 a DISTINCT workflow from guard shift scheduling (Shift records). WORKFLOW: Supervisor creates a TaskBatch allocated to a Control Room \u2192 tasks enter the Control Room queue (status 'queue') \u2192 Control Room Operator assigns \u2192 assigned user starts and performs SIGN-OFF 1 (status 'awaiting_verification' \u2014 NOT completed) \u2192 operator performs SIGN-OFF 2 verification (status 'completed' \u2014 requires BOTH sign-offs by DIFFERENT people) \u2192 immediate supervisor notification \u2192 deadline Task Completion Report. Recurring standalone tasks store a shared series id (recurrence_key) and parent_task_id; occurrences are generated server-side (bounded rolling window, deduplicated by recurrence_key). NULLABLE FIELDS: the gateway legitimately writes explicit nulls (unassigned tasks, optional site/times/notes, cleared fields) \u2014 plain string fields reject nulls on this platform, so these MUST declare type [\"string\",\"null\"]. TENANT ACCESS PATTERN: this entity deliberately carries NO {{user.data.*}} RLS rules \u2014 ALL tenant reads/writes go through the scheduledTaskAccess backend function, which resolves the caller's tenant server-side from their User record, enforces the TASK_SCHEDULING / OPERATIONS / COMPLETE_SECURITY module licence, validates control-room/site/assignee tenant membership, and fails closed with 403 for cross-tenant access. Direct client access below is platform-admin only.",
  "properties": {
    "customer_id": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Tenant/customer ID for multi-tenant isolation"
    },
    "reseller_id": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ]
    },
    "control_room_id": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ],
      "description": "Control Room whose queue this task is allocated to (Task Scheduling workflow). Null for legacy direct-assignment tasks."
    },
    "control_room_name": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ],
      "description": "Snapshot of the control room name at allocation time."
    },
    "task_batch_id": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ],
      "description": "TaskBatch (task list) this task belongs to. Null for legacy standalone tasks."
    },
    "task_batch_title": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ],
      "description": "Snapshot of the task list title for display/reporting."
    },
    "site_id": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ],
      "description": "Optional site/service area (shared platform infrastructure \u2014 Task Scheduling never REQUIRES the Sites module)."
    },
    "site_name": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ]
    },
    "title": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "description": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ],
      "description": "Detailed instructions"
    },
    "task_type": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "check_guard",
        "contact_site",
        "verify_patrol",
        "follow_up_incident",
        "review_alarm",
        "confirm_shift",
        "contact_customer",
        "other"
      ],
      "default": "other"
    },
    "priority": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "low",
        "medium",
        "high",
        "critical"
      ],
      "default": "medium"
    },
    "assigned_to": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ],
      "description": "User ID of the assigned Guard/User. Null while the task sits in the Control Room queue."
    },
    "assigned_to_name": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ]
    },
    "assigned_by": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ],
      "description": "User ID who created/allocated the task"
    },
    "assigned_by_name": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ]
    },
    "assigned_at": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ],
      "format": "date-time",
      "description": "Timestamp the Control Room Operator (or supervisor) assigned the task to the user."
    },
    "assigned_by_operator_id": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ],
      "description": "Control Room Operator who allocated the task (when allocated by an operator)."
    },
    "assigned_by_operator_name": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ]
    },
    "scheduled_date": {
      "type": "string",
      "format": "date",
      "description": "SAST calendar date the task is scheduled for (YYYY-MM-DD)"
    },
    "scheduled_time": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ],
      "description": "SAST local time (HH:MM) the task is scheduled for"
    },
    "scheduled_at": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ],
      "format": "date-time",
      "description": "UTC ISO instant derived from scheduled_date + scheduled_time at the SAST fixed offset (+02:00). Used for sorting."
    },
    "due_date": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ],
      "format": "date-time",
      "description": "Optional due deadline (UTC ISO). Open tasks past this point are swept to status 'overdue'."
    },
    "status": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "queue",
        "assigned",
        "in_progress",
        "awaiting_verification",
        "completed",
        "reopened",
        "overdue",
        "cancelled",
        "new",
        "acknowledged",
        "awaiting"
      ],
      "default": "queue",
      "description": "Lifecycle: queue (Control Room queue) \u2192 assigned \u2192 in_progress \u2192 awaiting_verification (guard sign-off done) \u2192 completed (BOTH sign-offs). Also reopened (operator rejected), overdue (deadline passed without both sign-offs), cancelled. Legacy standalone-task statuses (new/acknowledged/awaiting) remain valid for old records. ARCHIVED tasks keep their status \u2014 the archived flag hides them from active queues while preserving the full audit history."
    },
    "recurrence_type": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "none",
        "daily",
        "weekly",
        "weekdays",
        "monthly",
        "custom"
      ],
      "default": "none",
      "description": "Legacy standalone-task recurrence (TaskBatch-based scheduling is preferred)."
    },
    "recurrence_weekdays": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "number"
      },
      "default": []
    },
    "recurrence_interval_days": {
      "type": "number",
      "default": 1
    },
    "recurrence_end_date": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ],
      "format": "date"
    },
    "recurrence_key": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ],
      "description": "Series dedup key: '<seriesId>:<scheduled_date>'. Occurrence generation is idempotent."
    },
    "parent_task_id": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ],
      "description": "The series parent task id for generated occurrences."
    },
    "completion_notes_required": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "default": false
    },
    "completion_notes": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ],
      "description": "Guard/User completion notes (SIGN-OFF 1)"
    },
    "evidence_required": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "default": false,
      "description": "When true, the guard/user must attach evidence to sign off."
    },
    "completion_evidence_url": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ],
      "description": "Guard/User evidence file URL (SIGN-OFF 1)"
    },
    "completion_signature": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ],
      "description": "Guard/User digital signature (PNG data URL) \u2014 SIGN-OFF 1"
    },
    "completed_at": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ],
      "format": "date-time",
      "description": "Guard/User sign-off timestamp (SIGN-OFF 1)"
    },
    "completed_by": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ],
      "description": "Guard/User ID who signed off (SIGN-OFF 1)"
    },
    "completed_by_name": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ],
      "description": "Guard/User full name who signed off (SIGN-OFF 1)"
    },
    "verification_notes": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ],
      "description": "Control Room Operator verification notes (SIGN-OFF 2)"
    },
    "verification_signature": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ],
      "description": "Control Room Operator digital signature (PNG data URL) \u2014 SIGN-OFF 2, always a DIFFERENT person from SIGN-OFF 1"
    },
    "verified": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "default": false,
      "description": "True once the Control Room Operator has verified (SIGN-OFF 2)"
    },
    "verified_by": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ],
      "description": "Control Room Operator ID (SIGN-OFF 2)"
    },
    "verified_by_name": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ],
      "description": "Control Room Operator full name (SIGN-OFF 2)"
    },
    "verified_at": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ],
      "format": "date-time",
      "description": "Control Room Operator sign-off timestamp (SIGN-OFF 2)"
    },
    "final_completed_at": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ],
      "format": "date-time",
      "description": "Final completion timestamp \u2014 set ONLY when both sign-offs exist."
    },
    "non_completion_reason": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ],
      "description": "Mandatory reason captured for an outstanding/overdue task at (or after) the deadline."
    },
    "reason_captured_by": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ]
    },
    "reason_captured_by_name": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ]
    },
    "reason_captured_at": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ],
      "format": "date-time"
    },
    "reopen_reason": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ],
      "description": "Mandatory rejection reason when the operator rejects the guard/user completion. The task returns to the assigned user; the previous sign-off data and the full audit history are preserved."
    },
    "reopened_by": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ]
    },
    "reopened_by_name": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ]
    },
    "reopened_at": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ],
      "format": "date-time"
    },
    "last_reminder_at": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ],
      "format": "date-time",
      "description": "Timestamp of the last 2-hour outstanding-task reminder for this task."
    },
    "additional_notification_user_ids": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "string"
      },
      "default": [],
      "description": "Optional per-task override of the Task Batch's additional notification recipients (same customer only). Empty = inherit the batch recipients."
    },
    "related_entity": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ],
      "description": "Optional integration link (incident, maintenance, patrol, access activity) \u2014 integrations with other modules are OPTIONAL enhancements, never dependencies."
    },
    "related_id": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ]
    },
    "notes": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ]
    },
    "archived": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "default": false,
      "description": "DATA LIFECYCLE \u2014 ARCHIVE: hides this task from every active operational queue/view (operator queue, My Tasks, supervisor active lists, sweep reports) while PRESERVING the full record, both sign-offs, evidence, notes and audit history. Archived tasks stay searchable/viewable by authorised administrators under the Archived view and can be restored. Tasks with operational history (sign-offs/evidence/reasons/reports) must be archived, never destructively deleted \u2014 delete is only permitted for never-actioned tasks."
    },
    "archived_at": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ],
      "format": "date-time",
      "description": "Timestamp the task was archived (null when active or restored)."
    },
    "archived_by": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ],
      "description": "User ID of the administrator who archived this task."
    },
    "archived_by_name": {
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ],
      "description": "Display name of the administrator who archived this task."
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "customer_id",
    "title",
    "task_type"
  ],
  "rls": {
    "create": {
      "$or": [
        {
          "user_condition": {
            "role": "admin"
          }
        },
        {
          "user_condition": {
            "admin_level": "platform"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "read": {
      "$or": [
        {
          "user_condition": {
            "role": "admin"
          }
        },
        {
          "user_condition": {
            "admin_level": "platform"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "update": {
      "$or": [
        {
          "user_condition": {
            "role": "admin"
          }
        },
        {
          "user_condition": {
            "admin_level": "platform"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "delete": {
      "$or": [
        {
          "user_condition": {
            "role": "admin"
          }
        },
        {
          "user_condition": {
            "admin_level": "platform"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}